---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const GH = 'https://github.com/fudge-launcher/fudge';
const crates = [
  ['fudge-core', 'Query, result and action types, the provider trait, ranking, history, config.'],
  ['fudge-compute', 'The answers engine: calc, units, currency, time, emoji, colours. No I/O, and it compiles to WebAssembly (that is what powers the demo on this site).'],
  ['fudge-providers', 'Apps, files, windows, system commands, web search, shell and more.'],
  ['fudge-platform', 'Per-OS glue: hotkeys, window listing and focus, lock and sleep, open.'],
  ['apps/fudge', 'The GTK4 and libadwaita app, daemon and CLI.'],
];
const ideas = [
  'Add unit conversions or currency aliases to fudge-compute, with a golden test.',
  'Add city names to the time-zone table.',
  'Write a .desktop file or Wayland shortcut recipe for your desktop environment.',
  'Test the build on your distro and improve the dependency list.',
  'Report which Wayland compositor features work for you.',
  'Improve this website, or the docs.',
];
---
<Base title="Contribute to Fudge Launcher">
  <div class="page"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h1>Contribute</h1>
    <p>Fudge is MIT or Apache-2.0 and built in the open at <a href={GH}>github.com/fudge-launcher/fudge</a>. Contributions are licensed the same way.</p>
    <h2>Build and test</h2>
<pre><code>git clone {GH}.git
cd fudge
cargo build --release
cargo test --workspace</code></pre>
    <p>System packages for the GTK app are listed on the <a href="../install/">install page</a>. The answers engine and most logic tests need only Rust.</p>
    <h2>Code layout</h2>
    <ul>{crates.map(([n, d]) => <li><code>{n}</code>: {d}</li>)}</ul>
    <p>Planned later: an indexer crate, a plugin host crate and a settings app.</p>
    <h2>Good first issues, ideas</h2>
    <ul>{ideas.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>The site lives in <code>web/</code> (Astro, plain CSS). See <code>web/README.md</code>. To rebuild the demo's WebAssembly, run <code>web/scripts/build-wasm.sh</code>.</p>
  </div></div>
</Base>
